        <infoLink name="Rugged Plate" id="6c7a-d404-70c1-7d70" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="rule-rugged-plate"/>
        <infoLink name="Explosive End (D5&quot;)" id="b13f-536e-69fe-c476" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="rule-explosive-end"/>
        <infoLink name="Base 90x155" id="1493-8bdb-e2bc-90f8" hidden="false" type="profile" targetId="1da7-86f6-73a6-1bb5"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Combat Support Vehicle" id="9d8f-0a24-472a-6af0" hidden="false">
          <description>When this unit activates in the Combat Phase, instead of making any other action, if this unit is more than 6” from any enemy units it can repair one friendly *vehicle* within 3”. That unit may immediately take an attrition test.
A unit cannot both make repairs and tow other units in the same turn.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Chain Tow" id="be75-5864-11b7-959e" hidden="false">
          <description>If this unit did not move during the Movement Phase, instead of making any other action in the Combat Phase, it must select a non-*leviathan* *vehicle* within 3” of it to tow. It can then move up to 8”. When this unit finishes its move, the towed unit can be placed within 3” of it, but must be placed wholly within 8” of its original position.
Towed units cannot move or be moved by any other abilities in that phase, but do not count as having moved for the purposes of any abilities in subsequent turns.
Units may not make a tow move without towing another unit. A unit cannot both make repairs and tow other units in the same phase, and a towed unit cannot perform a tow in the same phase.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
